/target
# Cargo.lock IS committed here, on purpose -- score-jni links this crate's
# rlib into ITS shipped cdylib (the Spark JVM jar's native library), and
# this crate's own cdylib is separately built in CI as a verified artifact
# too ("Build the cdylib too" -- ci.yml). Its deps must NOT float. A fresh
# resolve on a checkout with no lock pulled tinyvec 1.13.0 (a real upstream
# regression: "cannot find macro `vec` in this scope") where 1.12.0 --
# already pinned here -- builds clean. Same rationale and same incident
# shape as packages/rust/extensions/.gitignore's datafusion-udf entry
# (brotli 8.0.3 there). The parent .gitignore's blanket `Cargo.lock` rule
# still applies to this directory unless explicitly negated here.
!Cargo.lock
